\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Part 1: is the silver/bronze standard better than GOI's own output?}{61}{paragraph*.208}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Part 2: once the silver standard existed, did tuning and fine-tuning the pipeline against it actually help?}{62}{paragraph*.210}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Limitation: precision is a lower bound, not an exact figure.}{64}{paragraph*.212}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A second, distinct bias: active-learning sampling skews which relevant companies get verified, not just how many.}{64}{paragraph*.214}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A third bias, harder to quantify: the author personally breaks judge disagreements, then those decisions score the author's own system.}{65}{paragraph*.216}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Future work: tightening this bound with more exhaustive LLM ranking.}{65}{paragraph*.218}%
